{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/266321.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS KENT-56C226: Kent-56C226. Roman. Coin. Romano-British imitation or barbarous copy. Obverse view."]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["moneta"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (moneta)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["268-273 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Kent (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Iscrizione o legenda"]},"value":{"none":["IMP[]"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["268-273AD. Romano-British - imitation of a Roman billon antoninianus or barbarous radiate. Length 17.0mm, Width 14.5mm, Thickness 1.9mm, Diameter 17.0mm, Weight 1.5g. Obverse: Crude radiate bust right. Inscription: IMP[]. Reverse: No details visible. Inscription: Illegible. Mint name: Britain by provenance. Very worn especially the reverse, rounded, rectangular flan, struck a little off centre. Variable green patina and some rusty brown surface deposit probably from water logged soil conditions. Ref. Coins of England and the UK, Spink 2009, page 78-79, Identifying Roman Coins, Richard Reece and Simon James, Seaby 1986, Reprint 1994, page 22-23 No. 24 or 25 and Roman Coins Found In Britain,…"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["KENT-56C226"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["266321"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: None, Geoff Burr, 2009-08-17 12:54:56, CC BY-SA 2.0 ; None, Geoff Burr, 2009-08-17 12:54:56, CC BY-SA 4.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefact